<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estonian Provincial Assembly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Maapäev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Estonian Provincial Assembly, or Maapäev, was the elected council of the Autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, created after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and first meeting in July 1917. On 28 November 1917 it declared itself the supreme authority in Estonia before Bolsheviks dispersed it. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-elders-carthage">Council of Elders</a> set up the Salvation Committee, which proclaimed the Republic of Estonia in February 1918.</p></div>
